=== PARITY (vs web TeslaChargingSessionsMap.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> NONE. The web source is a pure presentational leaf its parent (the charging list
    page) feeds a `sessions` prop; it owns no query. The native page mirrors this exactly: the model
    is seeded from the navigation-supplied sessions (TeslaChargingSessionsMapModel); the view performs
    NO HTTP. The single declared data state is `empty`; there is no `loading`/`error` source to
    fabricate (inventing them would be drift from the spec — same disposition as the TelemetryErrorsPanel
    leaf precedent), so they are deliberately not added.
  center -> SessionsMapProjector.center: average of every session's (lat ?? 0, lng ?? 0) (web `center`
    reduce), with the (37.77, -122.42) San Francisco fallback when empty. Non-finite guarded to 0.
    Executed unit tests pin both branches.
  clusterPoints -> SessionsMapProjector.marker: keeps only sessions with finite numeric lat AND lng
    (web `typeof === 'number' && !Number.isNaN`); resolves the site title or the localized Unknown
    (web `site_location_name || t(unknown)`); builds the popup detail lines (datetime, `fmtNumber(
    convertEnergyFromSI(wh,'kWh'),1)` kWh, `formatCurrency(cost,2)`, uppercased charger) under the same
    presence rules as the web template; and sets the aria label from the `{{name}} charging session`
    template. Verified by executed XCTest.
  Map (3 items) -> SessionsMapContainer composes the P3 MapKit wrappers natively (no WKWebView/Leaflet
    clone): MapContainer = MapKit `Map(position:)`; MapTileLayer = `.mapStyle(TSMapStyle.standard)`;
    MarkerCluster = client-side `SessionsMapClustering` (span-scaled grid, the native stand-in for
    Leaflet `maxClusterRadius=60`) rendered as `TSMarkerCluster` bubbles with `TSVehicleAnnotation`
    singletons. Tapping a marker opens its popup callout; tapping a cluster zooms toward it.
  States -> content (populated map) + empty (ContentUnavailableView when no session carried a usable
    coordinate; web would render a blank SF-centered map — the HIG-native page surfaces an empty state
    instead of a blank region). Each branch has a #if DEBUG preview; phase logic is unit-tested.
  i18n -> all 3 source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web `t(key,default)` fallback:
    tesla_sessions.mapLabel ("Charging sessions map"), tesla_sessions.markerLabel ("{{name}} charging
    session"), tesla_sessions.unknown ("Unknown") — ALL present in TeslaChargingSessionsMap.strings,
    plus 4 HIG-native chrome/a11y keys (empty title/message, cluster VoiceOver summary, callout close).
    No English literals in native code (Text(verbatim:) over the facade; unit symbols kWh/$ follow the
    ChargingSessionCard precedent).
  a11y -> the map container carries the role=application `mapLabel`; every marker carries the
    interpolated `markerLabel` + isButton; every cluster carries a localized "N charging sessions"
    summary + isButton; the callout combines its children; Dynamic Type via tokens; light/dark +
    increased-contrast via the generated dynamic colors. SI units honored (energy stored as Wh,
    converted to kWh only at the display boundary).
  Telemetry -> TeslaChargingSessionsMapModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface:"TeslaChargingSessionsMap")
    -> bridges the shared Telemetry.track (P1/S11). Asserted by a spy test (fires exactly once).
  Navigation -> chargingSessionsMapDestination() registers a NavigationStack destination for the
    TeslaChargingSessionsMapRoute value so a session list can push the full-screen map (the native
    affordance the unrouted web inline panel lacks); other pages are untouched (out of scope).

